# Etrata, Deadly Fugitive: "If you can't [turn it face up], exile it, then you may cast the exiled card without paying its mana cost." A cloaked instant card can't be turned face up (CR 701.58g, 701.40g). Etrata's combat
# damage on turn 3 cloaks Bot2's top card, Lightning Bolt: it stays face down. The granted ability ({2}{U}{B}) can't turn it face up, so it is exiled (CR 701.58a: the card goes to exile) and Bot1 casts the Bolt free,
# targeting Bot2: 20 - 1 (Etrata) - 3 = 16; the Bolt then goes to its owner's graveyard.

